# PRD, ADR, and slices

Product behaviour is defined by [`docs/prd.md`](../../docs/prd.md) and
[`docs/adr/`](../../docs/adr/), not improvisation.

## PRD

Every feature starts from `docs/prd.md` (the product as it is today) or a
feature PRD at `docs/prds/<feature>.md`.

- Copy [`docs/templates/prd-template.md`](../../docs/templates/prd-template.md).
- Scope, users, success criteria, and out of scope must be explicit.
- UI features list **Design references**: Mobbin screen links. Follow
  `.cursor/rules/mobbin-ui.mdc` before any HTML, CSS, or workspace chrome.

## ADR

Architecture and product decisions go in `docs/adr/NNNN-title.md`, numbered
from the next free integer. Follow
[`docs/adr/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md`](../../docs/adr/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md).
An accepted ADR is binding until a later ADR supersedes it.

## Slices

Split work into the smallest path that is complete (input → behaviour →
test → docs). Track each slice as a GitHub issue using
[`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/slice.yml`](../../.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/slice.yml).

Every slice issue includes:

- a user story
- Given / When / Then acceptance criteria (these are the TDD seams)
- a test plan
- out of scope
- **Design references** (Mobbin links) when the slice touches UI

One issue → one PR. Link the issue from the PR.
